WEBVTT

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:08.600
We'll find the owner.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:09.620
How, Robbie?

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:11.420
Let me think.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.100
Gemma, sit.

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:14.630
Good Gemma.

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:15.400
Give me your paw.

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:17.300
Good Gemma.

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:18.550
This dog is well trained.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:20.020
She likes you, too.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:22.020
So how are we going to find the owners?

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:24.690
With a little help from the ASPCA,

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:29.340
the American Society for the Prevention of Cruelty to Animals.

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:30.260
They're the ones.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:34.260
She was caught in the branches of our tree.

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:35.960
And Dad called the ASPCA.

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:37.860
They came and solved the problem.

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:39.240
Robbie, let's call them.

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:46.040
Let me see -- ASPCA...

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:52.180
Here it is.

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:53.960
ASPCA Animal Shelter.

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:57.240
555-7700.

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:17.580
Hello, my name is Robbie Stewart.

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:20.420
I have a lost dog I'd like to bring to you.

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:21.260
How late are you open?

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:24.150
Thank you.

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:25.720
I'll bring the dog over by nine.

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:26.410
Thanks.

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:26.920
Bye.

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:28.430
Thanks.

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:37.740
They're still open?

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.340
They're open until nine o'clock.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:40.800
We have two and a half hours.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.050
Let's take Gemma by there now.

00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:43.900
They'll find the owner.

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:46.440
I hope so.

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:50.020
I'm so sad to see this little dog without her family.

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:52.020
I'm sure they'll find the owner.

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:54.960
But if they don't, I'll adopt her.

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:57.040
She's so cute.

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:00.880
Look at those eyes.

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:03.920
She's hard to resist.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.060
Don't you just love her?

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:09.210
I'd like to keep her, too.

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:11.220
But I'll be going home to Greece

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:12.400
at the end of the semester.

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:15.920
She just wants love and affection.

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:20.620
Come on, Robbie.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:21.920
Let's get her to the animal shelter,

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:23.820
so they can find her owners quickly.

00:02:25.270 --> 00:02:26.600
Don't worry, Gemma.

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:27.560
We'll get you home.

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:30.020
It's not easy being away from home.

00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:31.590
Come on, poochie.

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:35.360
Let's go.

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:37.280
We're off to the animal shelter.

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:01.920
Your name?

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:03.100
Robbie Stewart.

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:05.520
And this is Alexandra Pappas.

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:07.860
Your name will do, Mr. Stewart.

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:11.720
Your address?

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:15.400
46 Linden street, Riverdale.

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:20.380
Where did you find the dog?

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:24.000
You tried calling the number on the collar?

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:27.300
Yes, but the number's no longer in service.

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:29.600
And there's no address on the dog tag?

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:31.600
There's no other information.

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:33.680
No ID number.

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:36.400
Without that, it's hard.

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:40.080
You will try to find the dog's owner.

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:42.520
Oh, we'll try, believe me.

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:44.640
And if you don't?

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:45.740
Yes?

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:51.680
Why, yes.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:54.900
If the owners don't claim the dog in forty-eight hours,

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:56.380
then you can apply for adoption.

00:03:57.020 --> 00:03:58.040
How do I do that?

00:03:58.120 --> 00:03:59.300
You really want to?

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:00.880
Yes, I'm serious.

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:03.380
If no one comes to claim Gemma,

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:04.660
I'd like to adopt her.

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:06.180
It's not difficult.
